+Session-row permission and form badges read the relevant directory-store buckets and show only whether something waits, without a count: one form can hold many questions, and a number that does not drop as the user answers them reads as wrong. A collapsed row covers its own pending requests and those of the descendants it hides; an expanded row covers only its own. Collapsed worktree, folder, group and run headers count their hidden sessions the same way, through `useCollapsedSessionActivityState`. The lookup never bootstraps a directory and never creates a store for one: it reads a store that already exists and leaves a directory nobody opened to the cross-directory index. Until a store's own request snapshots are ready, the row lookup also reads permissions and forms from that index, which the host seed fills at load, so a request already waiting in a project this client never opened still shows after a reload. Once they are ready, the store answers alone, so a form the index kept after a lost settlement stops showing. Mobile rows use the same lookup and icon-only badges: `MobileSessionRow` and `MobileSessionSwitcher` build their scopes with `selectBlockingBadgeSessionScopes`, the helper the desktop row and switcher use, so a session resolves its directory the same way on every surface. A session with no known directory has no store to answer for it, so the index still counts there, on the phone as on the desktop. A page an agent shows that waits for the user's answer has no directory-store bucket, so the row lookup also reads it from the cross-directory index and shows it as a form.
 
